        <article class="max-w-3xl">

          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-zinc-400">
            01 · 2024
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-zinc-950 sm:text-3xl">
            WiFi Received Signal Strength (RSS) Based Automated Attendance
            System for Educational Institutions
          </h2>

          <p class="mt-4 text-base text-zinc-500">
            <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-700">
              Sidratul Muntaha Khan
            </strong>,
            Mehreen Tabassum Maliha,
            Md Shahedul Haque,
            Ashikur Rahman
          </p>

          <p class="mt-2 text-base text-zinc-500">
            11th International Conference on Networking, Systems, and Security
            (NSysS '24)
          </p>

          <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-medium text-zinc-700">
            First Author · Research Lead
          </p>

          <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-zinc-600">
            Led the research and development of a smartphone-based automated
            attendance system using Wi-Fi received signal strength for
            zone-based indoor localization. The work investigated how Wi-Fi
            signal characteristics could be used to determine presence within
            defined indoor areas without relying on precise positioning,
            and evaluated the proposed approach through real-world deployment.
          </p>

